Snake arcade implementation — design decisions & rationale

WHY new `snake` modules + delete Hello (vs. in-place rename):
- Clean separation and clearer diff; migration history preserved via a
  forward migration (e31396db40b1 -> a1b2c3d4e5f6) rather than rewriting the
  original hello migration.

KEY DECISIONS:
- Board 20x20, initial snake length 3 => MAX_SCORE 397. This bound lives in
  BOTH schemas/snake.py and islands/snake/game.ts and MUST stay in sync; it
  doubles as an anti-spoofing guard on POSTed scores.
- Leaderboard order: score DESC, then earliest created_at, then id (stable,
  deterministic tie-breaker) — asserted in tests/test_snake.py.
- Score >= 1 required (only completed scoring runs stored). To make e2e
  deterministic AND yield a savable score, createInitialState() spawns the
  first food directly ahead of the head, so the opening rightward move always
  scores before the player steers into a wall.

GOTCHAS ENCOUNTERED:
- Pydantic custom field_validator raises ValueError, which lands in the error
  ctx and is NOT JSON-serializable. Fixed by serializing validation errors
  with e.errors(include_context=False, include_url=False) in views/snake.py.
- Dev Postgres alembic_version pointed at a dangling revision f1a2b3c4d5e6
  with zero tables; `flask db stamp/upgrade` errored. Recovered via a one-off
  `DELETE FROM alembic_version` then `flask db upgrade`.
- Pre-commit runs mypy in strict mode over STAGED test files (script/typecheck
  only covers src/). Test methods need `-> None`; the FlaskClient fixture is
  typed as `Any` because strict disallow_any_generics rejects the bare generic.
- Playwright strict-mode: player name renders in both the island and the
  server-rendered fallback leaderboard, so the reload assertion uses .first().

GAME LOOP: fixed-timestep via a ref-backed useInterval hook to avoid React
stale-closure bugs; keyboard input buffered in a ref and reversal-guarded on
each tick; arrow keys preventDefault to stop page scroll; listeners cleaned up
on unmount to prevent stacked controls across remounts.
